# config/tenant_keys.env.example — per-tenant runner API keys (ADR-010 M4)
#
# Copy to a LOCAL, GIT-IGNORED file and point the runner at it:
#     cp config/tenant_keys.env.example ~/.ai-cli-runner/tenant-keys.env
#     chmod 600 ~/.ai-cli-runner/tenant-keys.env        # keys are secrets
# (default path; override with $TENANT_KEYS_FILE). config/tenant_keys.env is also
# git-ignored if you prefer to keep it in-repo for a single machine.
#
# The per-tenant off-hours runner uses these to authenticate to the gateway as a
# specific tenant, so task pickup AND the review flip are scoped to that tenant
# server-side (tenantId derived from the credential, never a tool arg):
#     ./scripts/cli_task_runner.sh --tenant acme        # serve one tenant
#     ./scripts/cli_task_runner.sh --all-tenants        # sweep every tenant below
#
# Format — one tenant per line:  <tenantId>=<rawApiKey>   ( ':' also works )
# A real key looks like  myai_live_<43 base62 chars>  (or myai_test_… ).
#   • Get a tenant's key from dashboard signup (shown once) or `rotateApiKey`.
#   • Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored; surrounding whitespace trimmed.
#   • NEVER commit real keys. This .example file ships only placeholders.
#
# acme=myai_live_REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_KEY
# globex=myai_live_REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_KEY
#
# A line with an EMPTY key serves the local default tenant over the loopback
# default-trust path (no key needed on the gateway host) — handy to fold the
# single-operator queue into an --all-tenants sweep:
# default=
